EXPERIMENT 8: Process Memory Map

Theory:
- Process Memory Map: Represents the memory regions allocated to a process during execution.
- pmap: Displays the memory map of a process using its process ID (PID).
- Memory Regions: A process memory map may contain program code, data, heap, stack and shared libraries.
- pmap -x PID: Displays an extended memory map, including mapped memory, resident memory (RSS) and dirty memory.
- Resident Set Size (RSS): Amount of process memory currently residing in physical RAM.
- Dirty Memory: Memory pages that have been modified and may need to be written back to storage.

Commands
